{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776114644,"nonce":"oRc95ENzbxFnyeM5E5ILDkwHt/M=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM79ypsd","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/50","origin":"github"},"title":"Renumber subnets to N/N+1 (direct/VPN) scheme","message":"## Summary\n\nRenumber subnets to a consistent N (direct) / N+1 (VPN NETMAP) scheme across all network nodes. This simplifies DNS naming, eliminates per-boat operator NETMAP ranges, and makes the network layout easier to reason about.\n\n## Current Layout\n\n| Node | Direct | VPN NETMAP | Notes |\n|------|--------|------------|-------|\n| Ben | 192.168.10.0/24 | 192.168.11.0/24 | Original scheme |\n| Izzy | 192.168.12.0/24 | 192.168.14.0/24 | VPN is N+2, not N+1 |\n| Operator | 192.168.13.0/24 | 192.168.22.0/24 (bizzy), 192.168.15.0/24 (izzy) | Different NETMAP per boat |\n| Bizzy | 192.168.20.0/24 | 192.168.21.0/24 | Separate range |\n| Mobile Lab | 192.168.50.0/24 | — | On operator router |\n\n## Proposed Layout\n\n| Node | Direct (N) | VPN NETMAP (N+1) |\n|------|-----------|-----------------|\n| Ben | 192.168.10.0/24 | 192.168.11.0/24 |\n| Izzy | 192.168.12.0/24 | 192.168.13.0/24 |\n| Bizzy | 192.168.14.0/24 | 192.168.15.0/24 |\n| Operator | 192.168.50.0/24 | 192.168.51.0/24 |\n| Mobile Lab | TBD | — |\n\n## Benefits\n\n- VPN NETMAP is always N+1 — easy to remember\n- Single operator VPN NETMAP range (51) works from any boat\n- DNS convention becomes clean: `\u003chost\u003e.\u003cnetwork\u003e.p11.lan` / `\u003chost\u003e.vpn.\u003cnetwork\u003e.p11.lan`\n- No per-boat operator NETMAP ranges needed\n\n## Changes Required\n\n- Renumber bizzy LAN: 20→14, VPN: 21→15\n- Renumber operator LAN: 13→50, VPN: 22/15→51\n- Renumber izzy VPN: 14→13\n- Update DHCP, WireGuard allowed-IPs, firewall NETMAP rules on all routers\n- Update dnsmasq p11.hosts on all routers\n- Update static IPs on all devices\n- Resolve mobile_lab conflict at 192.168.50.0/24\n- Migration ordering matters (izzy VPN 14→13 must happen before bizzy direct →14)\n\n## Notes\n\n- WiFi bridge subnets (172.16.x) are unaffected\n- WireGuard tunnel endpoints (10.132.146.x) are unaffected\n- This is a significant renumbering — plan for a maintenance window\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}